ENTITY action_request_solution;
  method : action_method;
  request : versioned_action_request;
DERIVE
  description : text := get_description_value(SELF);
  name : label := get_name_value(SELF);
WHERE
  WR1: SIZEOF(USEDIN(SELF, 'BASIC_ATTRIBUTE_SCHEMA.' + 'DESCRIPTION_ATTRIBUTE.DESCRIBED_ITEM')) <= 1;
  WR2: SIZEOF(USEDIN(SELF, 'BASIC_ATTRIBUTE_SCHEMA.' + 'NAME_ATTRIBUTE.NAMED_ITEM')) <= 1;
END_ENTITY;



(*"action_request_solution"
An *action_request_solution* is an association between a
express_ref:[action_schema.versioned_action_request]
and an
express_ref:[action_schema.action_method]
that is a potential solution for the request.
*)


(*"action_request_solution.method"
the
express_ref:[action_schema.action_method]
that is a potential solution.
*)


(*"action_request_solution.request"
the
express_ref:[action_schema.versioned_action_request]
for which a solution is specified.
*)


(*"action_request_solution.description"

the
express_ref:[support_resource_schema.text]
that characterizes the *action_request_solution*.


NOTE: This attribute is an upwardly compatible addition to *action_request_solution* as specified in ISO 10303-41:1994.

*)


(*"action_request_solution.name"

the
express_ref:[support_resource_schema.label]
by which the *action_request_solution* is known.


NOTE: This attribute is an upwardly compatible addition to *action_request_solution* as specified in ISO 10303-41:1994.

*)

(*"action_request_solution.wr:WR1"

Each *action_request_solution* shall be the
express_ref:[basic_attribute_schema.description_attribute.described_item]
in at most one
express_ref:[basic_attribute_schema.description_attribute].


NOTE: The
express_ref:[basic_attribute_schema.description_attribute]
data type is defined in
express_ref:[basic_attribute_schema]
of this part of ISO 10303.

*)

(*"action_request_solution.wr:WR2"

Each *action_request_solution* shall be the
express_ref:[basic_attribute_schema.name_attribute.named_item]
in at most one
express_ref:[basic_attribute_schema.name_attribute].


NOTE: The
express_ref:[basic_attribute_schema.name_attribute]
data type is defined in
express_ref:[basic_attribute_schema]
of this part of ISO 10303.


NOTE: A template for constraining the population of the entity data types defined in the
express_ref:[basic_attribute_schema]
is described in annex E.

*)
